id: decisions/node
title: "decisions node"
kind: knowledge-node
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12"
updated: 2026-09-12

purpose: >
  Hold the decisions Dave has not yet made, as records he can ratify, reject,
  or correct. Each one is an axis on which the repository asserts both
  directions — some records prefer A, others prefer B — turned into one plain
  question, its options, the evidence on each side, an attributed
  recommendation, and what proof would show it is decided. Nothing here is
  decided by being written down.

principal_ref: principal:dave
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
inventory_ref: JUDGMENTS.md
id_index_ref: TAXONOMY.md
axis_ref: TAXONOMY.md

ranking_rule: >
  Records are numbered by leverage, highest first. leverage =
  judgments_resolved x split_weight x authored_conflict_bonus, where
  split_weight is 1.0 for a genuinely split axis, 0.7 leaning, 0.4 for a lone
  exception, and the bonus is 1.5 when both sides carry authored judgments (the
  repository contradicts itself in writing), 1.2 when one side does. The top
  record is next_question in records/yawn.bot-state.yawn. The formula is stated
  in every record so the rank can be argued with; rank is not importance,
  truth, obligation, or permission.

holds:
  - one decision-frame record per reversal axis, numbered by leverage
  - the container-intelligence naming question, held under the alias guard

receives:
  - the judgment inventory and its taxonomy
  - corrections and ratifications from Dave
  - new reversal axes when the inventory is rerun

produces:
  - next_question for the bot-state record and the Dave orientation page
  - a ratified decision, when Dave selects an option and names his authority
  - a stated rule or a written carve-out in the record the decision governs

lifecycle: >
  proposed -> Dave sets choice.selected_by, choice.option_ref, and
  choice.authority_ref -> the governing record is changed and the test named in
  proof_needed is added -> this record's status becomes superseded and points
  at the receipt. A decision Dave rejects stays here with status superseded and
  a one-line reason, so the question is not asked again fresh.

questions:
  - which decision, if answered, changes the most below it
  - which side of each axis do the tests already implement
  - what would it cost to write the exception down instead of removing it

boundary:
  - "desire cannot authorize action"
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective"
  - "ai output is not authority"
  - "a REVEALED judgment cited as evidence describes an artifact's behaviour, not Dave's choice"

proof:
  covers:
    - ranking_rule
    - lifecycle
  condition: >
    Every record in this folder carries authored_by, ratification_status,
    leverage equal to its printed formula inputs, numbering that follows
    leverage, an empty choice until Dave fills it, a recommendation with
    authority none, and judgment ids that resolve in TAXONOMY.md;
    tests/decisions.test.mjs checks each of these, tests/render-bot-state.test.mjs
    checks that a chosen or superseded decision leaves the queue, and
    tests/authored-by.test.mjs and tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs pass over
    this folder.
  tests:
    - tests/decisions.test.mjs
    - tests/render-bot-state.test.mjs
  source:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md
    - templates/decision.yawn
    - core/entity-and-coupling.yawn
  status: contract-defined
